=========== #515
#515 open Trim decoded horizons before combining forecast batches
When `predict_batch` processes separate batches with optional future covariates, `decode` can return the exact requested horizon for one batch and a patch-rounded horizon for another. Concatenating those outputs then raises a NumPy shape error. Trim each decoded batch to the requested horizon before collecting it.

The regression test covers mixed covariates, batch sizes 1–3, symmetric averaging, and padding modes. On the current `master`, 4 of its 12 cases fail with the concatenation error; all 12 pass with this change. Ruff passes.

